# Mogged

Windows PC games on Apple Silicon, launched from a Mac app. Open app → Play → game runs well. Users never see Windows, Wine, bottles, prefixes, GPTK, Proton, or VMs.

## Proof ladder

1. Free Steam smoke title launches from our shell (default: Aperture Desk Job).
2. Marvel's Spider-Man Remastered is the quality demo — not Elden Ring.
3. A second different-engine title later proves the pipeline, not a one-off.

## Build vs wrap

Do not write a Windows translation layer. Wrap Wine/CrossOver/D3DMetal. Our code is detection, `profiles/*.json`, shader/PSO cache, input, telemetry, and the Play UX.

## Speed

Phase numbers are order, not weeks. Take the shortest path to the next proof. Measure FPS; do not claim "feels native" without a benchmark file.
